The linear scan is replaced by a lazily-built, static 65536-entry direct lookup table indexed by message number, giving O(1) lookup instead of scanning all `MESGS` entries on every call. The table is built once (iterating backwards so the first matching entry wins, preserving identical semantics).
```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    static const std::array<const MESG*, 65536> table = [] {
        std::array<const MESG*, 65536> t{};
        for (int i = MESGS - 1; i >= 0; --i)
            t[mesgs[i].num] = &mesgs[i];
        return t;
    }();

    return table[num];
}
```
```include
#include <array>
```